      "type": "adventure",
      "x": 4200,
      "speaker": "Shepherd",
      "lines": [
        "Hoy! Off the ridge line — wind'll take you off it like a hat.",
        "Nobody comes over the top in this season. They go under, through the dark, and pay the toll to whatever lives in it.",
        "You came over the top. That's either courage or you've nobody left to be careful for."
      ],
      "choices": [
        "I'm looking for my family",
        "I took the safer road",
        "Say nothing"
      ],
      "responses": [
        "He is quiet a while. Then: a group came over this same ridge, before the snows. Worn thin. Asking after a child.",
        "He laughs, once, into the wind. Safer. Aye. That's one word for the high road in winter.",
        "He nods slowly, as if silence were the answer he expected, and points east with his crook."
      ],
